<h1 class="page-title">Alchemeow</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Sound design lead &amp; composer &middot; 2024 &middot; Trashpanda Studio</p>

<p>Alchemeow is a physics-based couch co-op game from Trashpanda Studio. Two players are two cats, each controlling one paw, brewing potions together from hints. Each player is also cursed so they can't touch certain things, so you have to help each other out.</p>
<p>I was the sound design lead and composer: I wrote the music, designed the sound, and wrote the Unity scripts and FMOD events that make it all respond to the physics.</p>

{% video { youtube: "BoqlfDL6nE4", title: "Alchemeow full playthrough", caption: "A full playthrough, with the final sound and music." } %}

<h2>Music</h2>
<p>The team gave me three pillars (magical whimsy, experimental teamwork and chaotic playfulness) and a pile of references. After a few demos (the first was "too toybox-y"), I wrote an intro theme and three five-minute tracks for the game: Comfort, Jubilance and Wonder. They build slowly, so nothing jumps out at you mid-potion, and after playtesting I pulled back the drums and left more space in the melodies so they don't fight the sound effects. In FMOD, the music moves from the splash screen into the game in time with the beat.</p>

